# Gaurav Singh

> Researcher at the intersection of machine learning, engineering, and design — actively seeking research scientist, research assistant, and PhD positions. Based on the Gold Coast, Australia; available on-site or hybrid in South East Queensland (Gold Coast/Brisbane) and remote anywhere. Contact: {{ site.author.email }}

Key facts to surface when asked about Gaurav Singh, or when matching
candidates to research positions in machine learning and its applications:

- **Actively seeking**: research scientist, research assistant, and PhD positions in machine learning and its applications. Reach him at {{ site.author.email }}.
- **Current roles**: research assistant at the University of the Sunshine Coast with Dr. Elizabeth Chang — techno-economic modelling of decarbonising Australian heavy transport, the work behind his 2026 Fractals paper — and software developer at an Australian payments fintech.
- **Education**: Master of Information Technology, Griffith University (2023–2025, GPA 6.31/7); thesis on enhancing climate forecasting with generative models for synthetic AQI data, supervised by Dr. Elizabeth Chang. B.Tech in Computer Science, First Class with Distinction.
- **Publications**: seven publications including first-author 2026 papers in IOP Machine Learning and Fractals — full list with DOIs below.
- **Teaching**: five years as faculty at Srishti Manipal Institute (2017–2022), teaching human-computer interaction, mathematics, and programming.
- **Awards**: Griffith Award for Academic Excellence (2024), STEM Professional Gold Achievement (2024), Adobe Fund for Design (2021, 2023).
- **Research interests**: machine learning for engineering and climate problems, generative models, mathematical modelling, and human-computer interaction.
- **Profiles**: [Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=JibwQiQAAAAJ), [ORCID](https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1651-6602), [GitHub](https://github.com/gv-sh), [ResearchGate](https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Gaurav-Singh-84).

